text She closes her eyes and readies her violin.
text The bow touches the strings much more carefully than before.
text It sounds different, I think.
text Maybe she's a little more relaxed. The music is still clumsy, but it's better than before.
text It feels like a small child trying her best to play.
text The bow moves up and down as if chasing the musical notes.
text Her left-hand fingers don't move much as they firmly grip the strings.
text The music is simple, yet warm.
text Why does the timbre of the violin always seem so nostalgic?
text While thinking that, I close my eyes.
